{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class P1575D {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n        int ans = solve(s);\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n\n    static int solve(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        if (n == 1) {\n            char c = s.charAt(0);\n            return (c == '0' || c == '_' || c == 'X') ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        char[] arr = s.toCharArray();\n        int total = 0;\n        if (!(arr[n-1] == 'X' && arr[n-2] == 'X')) {\n            total += tryEnding(arr, '2', '5');\n            total += tryEnding(arr, '5', '0');\n            total += tryEnding(arr, '7', '5');\n        }\n        if (arr[n-1] == 'X' && arr[n-2] == 'X') {\n            char[] copy = arr.clone();\n            put(copy, n-1, '0');\n            total += count(copy);\n        } else if (canPut(arr, n-1, '0') && canPut(arr, n-2, '0')) {\n            char[] copy = arr.clone();\n            put(copy, n-1, '0');\n            put(copy, n-2, '0');\n            total += count(copy);\n        }\n        return total;\n    }\n\n    static int tryEnding(char[] arr, char d2, char d1) {\n        int n = arr.length;\n        if (canPut(arr, n-1, d1) && canPut(arr, n-2, d2)) {\n            char[] copy = arr.clone();\n            put(copy, n-1, d1);\n            put(copy, n-2, d2);\n            return count(copy);\n        }\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    static boolean canPut(char[] s, int p, char d) {\n        char c = s[p];\n        return c == 'X' || c == '_' || c == d;\n    }\n\n    static void put(char[] s, int p, char d) {\n        if (s[p] == 'X') {\n            for (int i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n                if (s[i] == 'X') s[i] = d;\n            }\n        } else {\n            s[p] = d;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static int count(char[] s) {\n        int n = s.length;\n        int firstX = -1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (s[i] == 'X') {\n                firstX = i;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        int res = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            char c = s[i];\n            if (c == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) res *= 9;\n                else res *= 10;\n            } else if (c == 'X') {\n                if (i == firstX) {\n                    if (i == 0) res *= 9;\n                    else res *= 10;\n                }\n            } else if (i == 0 && c == '0') {\n                return 0;\n            }\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nbool canPut(const string& s, int p, char d) {\n    char c = s[p];\n    return c == 'X' || c == '_' || c == d;\n}\n\nvoid put(string& s, int p, char d) {\n    if (s[p] == 'X') {\n        for (int i = 0; i < (int)s.length(); i++) {\n            if (s[i] == 'X') s[i] = d;\n        }\n    } else {\n        s[p] = d;\n    }\n}\n\nint count(const string& s) {\n    int n = (int)s.length();\n    int firstX = -1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (s[i] == 'X') {\n            firstX = i;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    int res = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        char c = s[i];\n        if (c == '_') {\n            if (i == 0) res *= 9;\n            else res *= 10;\n        } else if (c == 'X') {\n            if (i == firstX) {\n                if (i == 0) res *= 9;\n                else res *= 10;\n            }\n        } else if (i == 0 && c == '0') {\n            return 0;\n        }\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint tryEnding(const string& arr, char d2, char d1) {\n    int n = (int)arr.length();\n    if (canPut(arr, n-1, d1) && canPut(arr, n-2, d2)) {\n        string copy = arr;\n        put(copy, n-1, d1);\n        put(copy, n-2, d2);\n        return count(copy);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint solve(const string& s) {\n    int n = (int)s.length();\n    if (n == 1) {\n        char c = s[0];\n        return (c == '0' || c == '_' || c == 'X') ? 1 : 0;\n    }\n    string arr = s;\n    int total = 0;\n    if (!(arr[n-1] == 'X' && arr[n-2] == 'X')) {\n        total += tryEnding(arr, '2', '5');\n        total += tryEnding(arr, '5', '0');\n        total += tryEnding(arr, '7', '5');\n    }\n    if (arr[n-1] == 'X' && arr[n-2] == 'X') {\n        string copy = arr;\n        put(copy, n-1, '0');\n        total += count(copy);\n    } else if (canPut(arr, n-1, '0') && canPut(arr, n-2, '0')) {\n        string copy = arr;\n        put(copy, n-1, '0');\n        put(copy, n-2, '0');\n        total += count(copy);\n    }\n    return total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    int ans = solve(s);\n    cout << ans << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0025880197063088417, -7.676783570786938e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.998623186722398e-05, -3.4689302992774174e-05,